{
  "$comment": [
    "The perf gate (plan §3.4, §11.3 G12). bench/ab.mjs and bench/compare.mjs read this file.",
    "ratio: the busy-time median-of-medians limit head/base on a set's scenarios (each scenario's primary metric), after raising both sides to floorMs.",
    "sets: the scenarios each milestone's merge must run (`bench:ab --set M<N>`); `default` is the §3.4 set used without --set; M14 runs everything.",
    "overrides: per-scenario ratio limits on a metric, for one set or every set (`*`).",
    "budgets: absolute targets on the head. kind `time` budgets are recorded as met/missed and block only in budgetsBlockIn (EXECUTION rule 3); kind `count` budgets (debug counters, fidelity, bytes) block in their sets.",
    "noise: a row is noisy when a round ran with the 1-minute load above cores × loadPerCore, or when one side's runs disagree by more than `spread` (max/min). A blocking failure on a noisy row is re-measured up to `retries` times (plan §3.4).",
    "A scenario that is in no set and in no budget is 'unlisted': compare fails on it unless --allow-new."
  ],
